# SmartCode .dockerignore
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS (this is not boilerplate): without it, `docker
# build`'s context includes whatever the HOST checkout currently has on
# disk - including a real, host-installed node_modules/ if `pnpm install`
# was ever run locally before `docker compose up --build`. The
# Dockerfiles' build stages do `COPY --from=deps /repo /repo` (the
# correctly container-installed dependency tree) and THEN
# `COPY apps/api apps/api` / `COPY apps/web apps/web` (source from the
# build context) - without this file, that second COPY silently
# overwrites the just-installed node_modules with whatever the host had,
# which may be for the wrong platform/libc, may contain broken symlinks
# (pnpm's structure differs meaningfully between Windows and Linux), or
# may simply be missing devDependencies if the host's last install used
# --prod. That mismatch is what produced:
#   "Cannot find module '/repo/apps/api/node_modules/prisma/build/index.js'"
# even though `pnpm install` had succeeded correctly in the deps stage
# moments earlier in the same build.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output - always rebuilt inside the container, never copied in
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
apps/api/dist/
apps/web/.next/

# Local env/secrets - never belong in an image
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Test artifacts
coverage/

# This project's own docs/scripts aren't needed inside either image
docs/
